WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.580
And how would you answer that for Tony?

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.630
What is something you admire about Tony?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.320
I think he's, um, reliable and loyal.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.260
Um, that's the one thing.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.720
So, you know, he doesn't change.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.730
If you see him, he'll be the same as he was last time, and he's consistent.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.420
I think that's the word I need.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.870
Um, but also his sense of humour. Hmm.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.400
As I mentioned before, that's the thing I find really good about him.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.660
I don't know why I like that sort of humour, because it's strange, but I do.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.590
It's the nicest thing anybody's ever said about me, that I'm consistent.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.920
I feel really motivated now.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.180
Best compliment ever.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.360
I said he motivated people, and I'm consistent.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.690
I'm probably the most boring person you've ever met, by the sound of it.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.040
So now we're moving on to a new part of the podcast,

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.800
and they're kind of challenge questions.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.300
So I will ask you a question,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.810
and you will either point to yourself or to the other person. Okay?

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:09.640
So please wait, I'll say three, two, one, and you'll do it. Okay? Alright.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.520
So who was the most mischievous when you were younger?

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.200
Wait for it.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.530
Okay. Ready? Three, two, one.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.900
You both think you were!

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.640
Why do you think you were the most mischievous, then?

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.838
I think I was into taking risks more, and so up to mischief, maybe. Mm.

00:01:30.288 --> 00:01:37.208
Like the speeding thing, and I was, you know, I used to like taking risks.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:39.488
Okay. And Tony, why do you think you were the most mischievous?

00:01:39.488 --> 00:01:43.628
Well, yeah, I was much more of a rule player,

00:01:43.628 --> 00:01:47.088
but I suppose, with my sense of humour,

00:01:47.088 --> 00:01:49.378
I tended to get myself into some difficulty,

00:01:50.468 --> 00:01:54.308
where people didn't realise I was not being serious. Mm.

00:01:54.308 --> 00:01:58.708
So, uh, that often got me into some difficult positions, really.

00:01:58.708 --> 00:02:00.868
Okay. Say no more.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.388
No more. I'm not saying any more.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.528
And, um, okay. Next one.

00:02:05.528 --> 00:02:07.128
Okay, next one.

00:02:07.128 --> 00:02:09.988
Who was the better student?

00:02:09.988 --> 00:02:13.488
Ready? Three, two, one.

00:02:13.488 --> 00:02:16.218
Okay.

00:02:16.228 --> 00:02:19.128
So Tony was the more academic person. Absolutely, absolutely.

00:02:19.128 --> 00:02:20.188
The rules.

00:02:20.188 --> 00:02:24.988
Because you listened to authority and, uh, yeah. Yeah.

00:02:24.988 --> 00:02:26.788
Okay. So, alright, interesting.

00:02:26.788 --> 00:02:27.648
Next one.

00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:29.478
Who is the funniest?

00:02:30.228 --> 00:02:31.148
Three, two, one.

00:02:31.148 --> 00:02:33.398
Okay.

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:35.528
Who is the most serious?

00:02:35.528 --> 00:02:38.408
Three, two, one.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:41.688
Yeah. You are quite serious, Dad.

00:02:41.688 --> 00:02:43.048
Very serious.

00:02:43.048 --> 00:02:44.908
I think that's why you balance out, maybe.

00:02:44.908 --> 00:02:48.568
Um, who talks the most?

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.718
Three, two, one.

00:02:51.168 --> 00:02:54.108
Oh, okay.

00:02:54.108 --> 00:02:55.728
Okay, interesting.

00:02:55.728 --> 00:03:00.408
Next up, who is the most adventurous?

00:03:00.408 --> 00:03:00.978
Oh, sorry.

00:03:01.008 --> 00:03:01.917
That's okay.

00:03:01.917 --> 00:03:03.677
Uh, yeah. So who were you pointing at?

00:03:03.677 --> 00:03:04.137
Me.

00:03:04.137 --> 00:03:05.417
Dad's the most adventurous.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.827
Yeah, definitely. Absolutely.

00:03:07.737 --> 00:03:10.967
I've done things that Tony's never done.

00:03:11.377 --> 00:03:14.807
Climbing and abseiling and…

00:03:15.277 --> 00:03:17.437
You're not into abseiling and stuff?

00:03:17.437 --> 00:03:19.717
I mean, I do it,

00:03:19.717 --> 00:03:24.517
but I wouldn't do it with the enthusiasm that Ian has for it.

00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:26.317
I mean, I can do things like that. Mm.

00:03:26.317 --> 00:03:31.157
But I don't put myself forward to do it, really.

00:03:31.157 --> 00:03:33.687
Are you quite risk-averse, would you say?

00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:35.377
I would say so. Yeah. I am too. Yeah.

00:03:35.377 --> 00:03:41.087
So, I mean, another example is I've done some skiing,

00:03:42.017 --> 00:03:46.357
and I've really enjoyed that skiing, and I've been a few more times since.

00:03:46.357 --> 00:03:48.097
But if it hadn't have been for Ian…

00:03:48.097 --> 00:03:51.737
To be fair, I had skied before,

00:03:51.737 --> 00:03:54.917
but it was really he and the group that he'd

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:58.737
got around him that sort of got me into it, really.

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:02.797
Am I right in saying you met your wife on a skiing trip?

00:04:02.797 --> 00:04:03.657
That's correct. Yeah.

00:04:03.657 --> 00:04:04.717
You met her on a skiing trip?

00:04:04.717 --> 00:04:05.627
I did, yeah.

00:04:05.717 --> 00:04:07.417
Yes, that's true.

00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:11.177
But again, it was other people that were encouraging.

00:04:11.177 --> 00:04:13.797
It was a group thing.

00:04:13.797 --> 00:04:18.277
I don't think I'd have thought about going skiing on my own.

00:04:18.277 --> 00:04:20.137
You have Mr. Motivator over here.

00:04:20.137 --> 00:04:20.897
That's true.

00:04:20.897 --> 00:04:25.097
Um, okay.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:28.157
This is a bit of a controversial one,

00:04:28.157 --> 00:04:31.305
but let's just do it, you know, it's all good fun.

00:04:31.305 --> 00:04:35.215
Um, next is, who is the most stubborn?

00:04:37.765 --> 00:04:41.115
Ready. Three, two, one, go.

00:04:41.725 --> 00:04:42.905
Oh, there we go. Oh, okay.

00:04:42.905 --> 00:04:45.435
I think maybe you're just trying to be nice.

00:04:45.925 --> 00:04:47.585
Well, I don't think I'm very nice. No, no.

00:04:47.505 --> 00:04:52.355
I think I can be very fixed about certain things, so.

00:04:53.885 --> 00:04:55.005
I feel the same.

00:04:55.005 --> 00:04:58.995
I feel I can be very, very stayed in my ways.

00:04:59.325 --> 00:05:02.755
I don't like change a lot, so therefore I tend to, um,

00:05:03.885 --> 00:05:05.405
I can dig my heels in and be

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:08.425
stubborn about something I don't really want to do.

00:05:08.425 --> 00:05:10.265
Great phrase, to dig your heels in.

00:05:10.265 --> 00:05:10.795
Yeah.

00:05:11.145 --> 00:05:16.355
Tony, you're coming up with loads of fantastic idiomatic expressions today, so thank you.

00:05:16.965 --> 00:05:19.855
I talk in idiosyncrasies all the time. Um, alright.

00:05:21.065 --> 00:05:25.255
Next is, who would survive the longest on a desert island?

00:05:26.945 --> 00:05:29.885
Ready? Three, two, one, go.

00:05:29.885 --> 00:05:30.455
Oh.

00:05:30.865 --> 00:05:33.125
Why do you think you wouldn't survive the longest, then, Tony?

00:05:33.125 --> 00:05:37.125
Uh, I don't think I'm as resourceful as Ian is, to be honest.

00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:38.205
Alright. Right.

00:05:38.205 --> 00:05:43.245
And I'm also, if you look at all the things I do in terms of sport,

00:05:43.245 --> 00:05:45.465
I like people around me.

00:05:45.465 --> 00:05:46.865
I'm a group activity and group people,

00:05:46.865 --> 00:05:52.305
group things encourage me to do things I wouldn't otherwise do.

00:05:52.305 --> 00:05:56.845
Ian's much more solitary, but much more self-sufficient in that sense.

00:05:56.845 --> 00:05:59.685
He can do things for himself a lot more than I am.

00:05:59.685 --> 00:06:00.555
Yeah.
